es, particularly in surgical patients and those with chronic illnesses, by preventing malnutrition and promoting healing [Data: Reports (1214); Entities (547, 12902); Relationships (3803, 3700, 3739)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Impact of surgical procedures on nutritional needs\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Surgical procedures such as duodenopancreatectomy and gastrectomy often necessitate specialized nutritional management to support recovery. These surgeries can alter the digestive system's functionality, making it essential to tailor nutritional support to meet the unique needs of patients post-operation. The integration of nutritional support into surgical protocols, such as Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS), is critical for optimizing patient outcomes and minimizing complications [Data: Reports (1214); Entities (12591, 6006); Relationships (19199, 3759)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Nutritional support for critically ill patients\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Critically ill patients often require intensive nutritional support to address their unique dietary needs and prevent malnutrition. Conditions such as pancreatitis, cancer, and acute renal failure necessitate careful monitoring and management of nutritional intake. The provision of tailored nutritional interventions can significantly enhance recovery and improve overall health outcomes for these vulnerable populations [Data: Reports (1214); Entities (10110, 12907); Relationships (3733, 3707, 3731)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"The importance of multidisciplinary approaches\",\n            \"explanation\": \"A multidisciplinary approach to nutritional support is essential for effectively managing patients with complex health needs. This includes collaboration among dietists, physicians, and other healthcare professionals to ensure that nutritional interventions are tailored to individual patient requirements. Such te